  "content": "7.4 Magnitude earthquake strikes the Philippines\nOnlinekhabar\nFriday, October 10, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 10\nA powerful earthquake has struck Mindanao, the Philippines. According to the United States Geological Survey (USGS), the quake measured 7.4 in magnitude.\nA tsunami warning has been issued following the tremor.\nEarlier, on September 30, a 6.9 magnitude earthquake hit Cebu province in the Philippines, killing 69 people and injuring around 150 others.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nBP Highway\nFlowers\nnational women team\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nEarthquake jolts Gorkha\n1 month ago\nAfghanistan earthquake: Death toll reaches 622, Over 1,500 Injured\n1 month ago\nMagnitude 4.3 earthquake jolts Mugu again\n3 months ago\nEarthquake strikes Jajarkot\n5 months ago\nEarthquake strikes Sindhupalchok as Nepal marks 2015 quake anniversary\n6 months ago\nA decade after the quake: Are we safer, or simply forgetful?\n6 months ago\nMost Read\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\n12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces 